Assembly
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/foundry]

FIXME(horror): Workers stand at a bench inside the lamp's circle, hands moving on the same small clockwork assembly, unhurried and exact. Beyond the circle, only sound: shuffle and click in every direction, more hands than the dark will give up.
FIXME(horror): They wear the same drab uniform, the same cropped haircut, men and women alike, every age from the very young to the very old. When one of them tilts toward the light, the eyes that catch it are Suhail's: the Color tinged and burning, the same purple beyond purple, in face after face.
FIXME(horror): You speak to the woman nearest you. Nothing answers. Out of the black, Suhail's voice, delighted: "SHE CAN'T HEAR YOU." The words echo in the space; the room must be enourmous, vast and full of unseen work.
FIXME(dread): Suhail knocks her bin of pins across the ground. She stumbles after the scattered parts, untroubled, and slowly starts gathering the individual pins back up. "Nothing minds. They only tidy." 

choices:

* Set her work right = Sort the pins back, steady her hands
    FIXME(mundane): You gather the scattered pins and set the work straight. It costs nothing. She resumes as though nothing had happened. Suhail watches your face, not the work.
    +quality foundry.challenge 1
    +open "The Factory Floor"

* Leave her to it = Let her gather her own work
    FIXME(dread): You do nothing. She toils away on the ground and fades into darkness as the lantern's light leaves. You think you see Suhail grin briefly, but you can't be sure.
    +open "The Factory Floor"
